{
  "standard": "1.2.0",
  "section": "3.1, 5.20",
  "status": "normative",
  "description": "The grounding check of STANDARD v1.2 §5.20 for one host output under one grounding policy, with the evidence anchors of §6.5. An executor that accepts grounding@1, and a safety layer that applies grounding policies, MUST give the status and code each vector expects (§10.3). The policy's require is left out: each vector is an output of a capability the policy requires. Run by core/tests/grounding.rs (grounding::check), tests/test_grounding.py (_core.check_grounding and grounded_agency.grounding.check_output) and packages/acs-core/test/evidence.test.ts (checkGrounding). The message is not compared.",
  "fields": {
    "name": "Unique in this file.",
    "about": "What the vector covers.",
    "output": "The host's output. It already has every field its capability's contract requires (R402 is checked before grounding).",
    "policy": "The policy's kinds (a list, or null when the policy has none) and attested.",
    "bound_refs": "The references the step's input_bindings make, as bodies without ${, } and an annotation; for a call, its argument names.",
    "evidence_seen": "The Output response's evidence_seen, or null when it is absent.",
    "expect": "status: grounded, inferred or refused; code: null or F505. For a grounded or inferred output, counted (the anchors that count) and legacy (the items that are not evidence anchors)."
  },
